Homepage: https://github.com/yorkane/OpenCodex
Description: OpenCodex gateway and launcher
 OpenCodex is a middleware layer that exposes a machine's Codex Desktop
 runtime through a browser, so a phone, tablet or another computer can drive
 the same Codex session over the LAN or a tunnel.
 .
 This package installs the gateway, the web shell, the bundled patches
 (site branding, outbound host policy, headless Electron flags) and the
 production Node dependency closure, registers the Xvfb virtual display and
 the gateway systemd services, and provides the opencodex-gateway launcher
 for starting, stopping and opening the web UI.
 .
 Dependencies mirror the official ChatGPT desktop package, so installing this
 package also prepares everything the Codex Desktop runtime needs.
 .
 Node.js 22 or 24 is required (the runtime and the official Codex Desktop both
 run on it). Debian/Ubuntu 22.04 ships Node 12, so configure the NodeSource
 repository first, or install a package variant that bundles the runtime debs
 in its payload directory (see deploy.md).
 .
 The Codex Desktop runtime itself (the official chatgpt package, or a community
 converted directory) must be provided separately: point CODEX_DESKTOP_APP_PATH
 and CODEX_DESKTOP_EXECUTABLE_PATH in /etc/opencodex/gateway.env at it. To ship
 it offline, build with a payload directory (see deploy.md).
 .
